    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="_15-dot-matrix-module" tabindex="-1">15. Dot Matrix Module <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-dot-matrix-module" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15. Dot Matrix Module&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="_15-1-introduction" tabindex="-1">15.1 Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-1-introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15.1 Introduction&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The dot matrix module features high brightness, flicker-free rendering, and simple cable connections. It provides versatile visual display capabilities for numbers, text strings, and custom graphic symbols.</p><img loading="lazy" height="348" width="581" src="' + _imports_0 + '" class="common_img" style="width:300px;"><h2 id="_15-2-technical-specifications" tabindex="-1">15.2 Technical Specifications <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-2-technical-specifications" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15.2 Technical Specifications&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:center;">Parameter</th><th style="text-align:center;">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Operating voltage</td><td style="text-align:center;">5 V</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Operating current</td><td style="text-align:center;">45 mA</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Matrix resolution</td><td style="text-align:center;">8 × 16 pixels</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Brightness levels</td><td style="text-align:center;">8 adjustable levels</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Connector model</td><td style="text-align:center;">5264-4AW</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Mounting compatibility</td><td style="text-align:center;">LEGO-compatible hole spacing</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Dimensions</td><td style="text-align:center;">55.4 × 23.4 × 19.0 mm</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="_15-3-hands-on-project" tabindex="-1">15.3 Hands-On Project <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-3-hands-on-project" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15.3 Hands-On Project&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_15-3-1-project-introduction" tabindex="-1">15.3.1 Project Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-3-1-project-introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15.3.1 Project Introduction&quot;">​</a></h3><p>This project programs the dot matrix module to cycle through text strings, numbers, and custom graphic icons. Configuring screen brightness introduces essential display blocks while illustrating output methods across text, numeric, and graphical data formats.</p><h3 id="_15-3-2-hardware-wiring" tabindex="-1">15.3.2 Hardware Wiring <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-3-2-hardware-wiring" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15.3.2 Hardware Wiring&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Connect the dot matrix module to port <strong>A</strong> of the controller using a 4-pin module cable.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="418" width="1040" src="' + _imports_1 + '" class="common_img" style="width:500px;"><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>This module supports connection to any port among A, B, C, or D on the controller. Ensure that the port selected in the program matches the physical wiring.</strong></p></div><h3 id="_15-3-3-adding-extensions" tabindex="-1">15.3.3 Adding Extensions <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-3-3-adding-extensions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15.3.3 Adding Extensions&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Select <strong>Dot matrix module</strong> under the <strong>Output module</strong> category.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="1040" width="1920" src="' + _imports_2 + '" class="common_img" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_15-3-4-complete-program-and-analysis" tabindex="-1">15.3.4 Complete Program and Analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-3-4-complete-program-and-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15.3.4 Complete Program and Analysis&quot;">​</a></h3><ol><li><p>Set the brightness of the dot matrix module on port A to 8.</p></li><li><p>Inside the loop, continuously cycle through the display sequence:</p><ul><li><p>Display the text &quot;Hi&quot; at coordinates (0, 0) and wait 1 second.</p></li><li><p>Display the number 123 and wait 1 second.</p></li><li><p>Draw a heart pattern and wait 1 second, then repeat the sequence.</p></li></ul></li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="519" width="837" src="' + _imports_3 + '" class="common_img" style="width:500px;"><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>The source files are available for download under <a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1fLfLXEVjSMZdojOq7C44xJqZIBm4MDem?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Program Files/ 15 Dot Matrix Module.sb3</a>.</strong></p></div><h3 id="_15-3-5-program-upload" tabindex="-1">15.3.5 Program Upload <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-3-5-program-upload" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15.3.5 Program Upload&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Click <strong>Connect device</strong>, select the serial port, then click the upload button. Wait for the upload success notification to complete the program transfer.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="360" width="640" src="' + _imports_4 + '" class="common_img" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_15-3-6-program-outcome" tabindex="-1">15.3.6 Program Outcome <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-3-6-program-outcome" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15.3.6 Program Outcome&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Once the program upload is complete, the dot matrix screen continuously cycles through multiple display modes. The screen presents the text string &quot;Hi&quot;, transitions after a 1-second pause to the number 123, and then waits another second to draw a heart icon. This ongoing sequence highlights the dynamic display capabilities of the dot matrix module.</p>', 25)
